From d070b88dafdf15a02c54d3cb77c4b4663f00ea50 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: MiraWells <1020080523@qq.com>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 02:54:37 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] feat(hotstuff): stamp the EIP-7843 slot number and gate
 MobileRegistryRoot behind it

Ethereum's Amsterdam header has slot_number at RLP element 23, so
MobileRegistryRoot is element 24 (65f2c63f). The layout is now purely
fork-gated: from Glamsterdam, gov5's Amsterdam fork, a native-chain header
carries SlotNumber at 23, and MobileRegistryRoot at 24 when MobileAnchor is
also active (params.IsMobileRegistryRootInHeader). A MobileAnchor time
earlier than Glamsterdam takes effect at Glamsterdam; a header never carries
the root without the slot.

The slot is the block number: a HotStuff chain has views, not slots, the
view is not visible to an Ethereum client outside Extra, and the number is
what the Rust client already writes into its V4 payloads and sealed headers.
FinalizeAndAssemble stamps it; verifyHeader requires it from Glamsterdam,
equal to the number, and refuses it before. The miner and verifyHeader gate
the root on both forks.

Headers chain 94 sealed since mobileAnchorTime (root at element 23, no slot)
are not readable under this layout; that history is rebuilt with replay-v2
under the new fork schedule.
